18 rule(s), 3 subject(s), 3 polic(y/ies), compiled from 3 contract revision(s)
write the fragment: `zenctl acl gen --enrollment … --contracts … --json5 > router-acl.json5`, merge it at the router config's top level, restart the router, and regenerate on every contract revision (spec §11.2)

```

`--json5` is the deliverable: the fragment `zenohd` reads, field for field
zenoh 1.10, a comment per rule naming the grant it instantiates and the
fact it exists for. A foreign schema, so `--format` has no say over it.

```console
$ zenctl acl gen --enrollment ../examples/zk2/acl/tcgui.enrollment.toml --contracts ../examples/zk2/.history --json5
// zenohd access control, generated by `zenctl acl gen` (zk2 spec §11).
// namespace ""; default_permission deny; 3 subject(s), 18 rule(s), 3 polic(y/ies).
// Compiled from tc.netem.v1@sha256:30b491116ef6a534a3533741dc4003fe332c52ec84fcadcbd5dfa6f1be866245, tc.netif.v1@sha256:4f531ebec4c4eee015c18f11aefbce9138b413cfdca6bf6b777ea0eb6f43b4e0, tc.scenario.v1@sha256:2cc3d6047fe9a031d571740068e1eb0ca2eddb0fd2f86c4b7988f1d2f34caa3c: regenerate on every contract revision (§11.2).
// Field names: zenoh 1.10 (zenoh-config-1.10.1/src/lib.rs: AclConfig, AclConfigRule,
// AclMessage, InterceptorFlow, AclConfigSubjects, AclConfigPolicyEntry). Merge at the
// router config's top level; rules, subjects and policies are all required. Subjects
// are bound by usrpwd user names (transport/auth/usrpwd) or certificate CNs (mTLS),
// never zids (§11.3). Access control is enforced per hop, and the running block is not
// observable on the bus (§11.3): `zenctl acl gen --check --against` reads this file.
access_control: {
  enabled: true,
  default_permission: "deny",  // §11.2: grants compile to allow rules (RECOMMENDED)
  rules: [
    // own (h-3fa9c2d41b7e/tc): §11.1 Own: the service puts, deletes, serves and declares tokens under its prefix, each verbatim subtree spelled out because `**` never crosses one (§1.3), its `@adv` subtrees where it uses advanced publication (§2.5); reply covers its answers to queries on its own keys
    { id: "own-in:h-3fa9c2d41b7e/tc", permission: "allow", flows: ["ingress"],
      messages: ["put", "delete", "declare_queryable", "reply", "liveliness_token"],
      key_exprs: ["zk2/h-3fa9c2d41b7e/tc/**", "zk2/h-3fa9c2d41b7e/tc/*/@stream/**", "zk2/h-3fa9c2d41b7e/tc/*/@state/**", "zk2/h-3fa9c2d41b7e/tc/*/@op/**", "zk2/h-3fa9c2d41b7e/tc/@zk/**"] },
    // own (h-3fa9c2d41b7e/tc): §11.1 Own, egress: queries and subscriptions on its own keys reach it, so a queryable is asked and a publisher learns of interest (spike S14)
    { id: "own-out:h-3fa9c2d41b7e/tc", permission: "allow", flows: ["egress"],
      messages: ["query", "declare_subscriber"],
      key_exprs: ["zk2/h-3fa9c2d41b7e/tc/**", "zk2/h-3fa9c2d41b7e/tc/*/@stream/**", "zk2/h-3fa9c2d41b7e/tc/*/@state/**", "zk2/h-3fa9c2d41b7e/tc/*/@op/**", "zk2/h-3fa9c2d41b7e/tc/@zk/**"] },
    // fan_in (h-3fa9c2d41b7e/tc): §11.2: egress is checked by inclusion against the query's or subscription's own key expression, so every consumer or caller selector that intersects this provider's keys, and that its own patterns do not include, is granted here; without it a fan-in GET gets 0 replies (spike S14)
    { id: "fan-in:h-3fa9c2d41b7e/tc", permission: "allow", flows: ["egress"],
      messages: ["query", "declare_subscriber"],
      key_exprs: ["zk2/*/tc/tc.netem.v1/events/**", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netem.v1/state/**", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netem.v1/stream/**", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netif.v1/state/**", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netif.v1/stream/**", "zk2/*/tc/tc.scenario.v1/state/**", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netif.v1/@op/diagnostics", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netif.v1/@op/interfaces/*/*/set", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netem.v1/@op/config/*/*/set", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netem.v1/@op/plug/*/*/set", "zk2/*/tc/tc.scenario.v1/@op/execution/*/*/control", "zk2/*/tc/tc.scenario.v1/@op/scenarios/put", "zk2/*/tc/tc.scenario.v1/@op/scenarios/*/remove"] },
    // fan_in_reply (h-3fa9c2d41b7e/tc): §11.2: the same selectors for this provider's ingress reply, refusals included. An error reply (O2's fanout_forbidden, O3's unavailable) carries no key and is checked against the selector; a value reply is checked against its own key, which Own includes (measured, #612 FJ7)
    { id: "fan-in-reply:h-3fa9c2d41b7e/tc", permission: "allow", flows: ["ingress"],
      messages: ["reply"],
      key_exprs: ["zk2/*/tc/tc.netem.v1/events/**", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netem.v1/state/**", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netem.v1/stream/**", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netif.v1/state/**", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netif.v1/stream/**", "zk2/*/tc/tc.scenario.v1/state/**", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netif.v1/@op/diagnostics", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netif.v1/@op/interfaces/*/*/set", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netem.v1/@op/config/*/*/set", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netem.v1/@op/plug/*/*/set", "zk2/*/tc/tc.scenario.v1/@op/execution/*/*/control", "zk2/*/tc/tc.scenario.v1/@op/scenarios/put", "zk2/*/tc/tc.scenario.v1/@op/scenarios/*/remove"] },
    // own (h-20609002f7b6/tc): §11.1 Own: the service puts, deletes, serves and declares tokens under its prefix, each verbatim subtree spelled out because `**` never crosses one (§1.3), its `@adv` subtrees where it uses advanced publication (§2.5); reply covers its answers to queries on its own keys
    { id: "own-in:h-20609002f7b6/tc", permission: "allow", flows: ["ingress"],
      messages: ["put", "delete", "declare_queryable", "reply", "liveliness_token"],
      key_exprs: ["zk2/h-20609002f7b6/tc/**", "zk2/h-20609002f7b6/tc/*/@stream/**", "zk2/h-20609002f7b6/tc/*/@state/**", "zk2/h-20609002f7b6/tc/*/@op/**", "zk2/h-20609002f7b6/tc/@zk/**"] },
    // own (h-20609002f7b6/tc): §11.1 Own, egress: queries and subscriptions on its own keys reach it, so a queryable is asked and a publisher learns of interest (spike S14)
    { id: "own-out:h-20609002f7b6/tc", permission: "allow", flows: ["egress"],
      messages: ["query", "declare_subscriber"],
      key_exprs: ["zk2/h-20609002f7b6/tc/**", "zk2/h-20609002f7b6/tc/*/@stream/**", "zk2/h-20609002f7b6/tc/*/@state/**", "zk2/h-20609002f7b6/tc/*/@op/**", "zk2/h-20609002f7b6/tc/@zk/**"] },
    // fan_in (h-20609002f7b6/tc): §11.2: egress is checked by inclusion against the query's or subscription's own key expression, so every consumer or caller selector that intersects this provider's keys, and that its own patterns do not include, is granted here; without it a fan-in GET gets 0 replies (spike S14)
    { id: "fan-in:h-20609002f7b6/tc", permission: "allow", flows: ["egress"],
      messages: ["query", "declare_subscriber"],
      key_exprs: ["zk2/*/tc/tc.netem.v1/events/**", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netem.v1/state/**", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netem.v1/stream/**", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netif.v1/state/**", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netif.v1/stream/**", "zk2/*/tc/tc.scenario.v1/state/**", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netif.v1/@op/diagnostics", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netif.v1/@op/interfaces/*/*/set", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netem.v1/@op/config/*/*/set", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netem.v1/@op/plug/*/*/set", "zk2/*/tc/tc.scenario.v1/@op/execution/*/*/control", "zk2/*/tc/tc.scenario.v1/@op/scenarios/put", "zk2/*/tc/tc.scenario.v1/@op/scenarios/*/remove"] },
    // fan_in_reply (h-20609002f7b6/tc): §11.2: the same selectors for this provider's ingress reply, refusals included. An error reply (O2's fanout_forbidden, O3's unavailable) carries no key and is checked against the selector; a value reply is checked against its own key, which Own includes (measured, #612 FJ7)
    { id: "fan-in-reply:h-20609002f7b6/tc", permission: "allow", flows: ["ingress"],
      messages: ["reply"],
      key_exprs: ["zk2/*/tc/tc.netem.v1/events/**", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netem.v1/state/**", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netem.v1/stream/**", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netif.v1/state/**", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netif.v1/stream/**", "zk2/*/tc/tc.scenario.v1/state/**", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netif.v1/@op/diagnostics", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netif.v1/@op/interfaces/*/*/set", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netem.v1/@op/config/*/*/set", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netem.v1/@op/plug/*/*/set", "zk2/*/tc/tc.scenario.v1/@op/execution/*/*/control", "zk2/*/tc/tc.scenario.v1/@op/scenarios/put", "zk2/*/tc/tc.scenario.v1/@op/scenarios/*/remove"] },
    // own (h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend): §11.1 Own: the service puts, deletes, serves and declares tokens under its prefix, each verbatim subtree spelled out because `**` never crosses one (§1.3), its `@adv` subtrees where it uses advanced publication (§2.5); reply covers its answers to queries on its own keys
    { id: "own-in:h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend", permission: "allow", flows: ["ingress"],
      messages: ["put", "delete", "declare_queryable", "reply", "liveliness_token"],
      key_exprs: ["zk2/h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend/**", "zk2/h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend/*/@stream/**", "zk2/h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend/*/@state/**", "zk2/h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend/*/@op/**", "zk2/h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend/@zk/**"] },
    // own (h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend): §11.1 Own, egress: queries and subscriptions on its own keys reach it, so a queryable is asked and a publisher learns of interest (spike S14)
    { id: "own-out:h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend", permission: "allow", flows: ["egress"],
      messages: ["query", "declare_subscriber"],
      key_exprs: ["zk2/h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend/**", "zk2/h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend/*/@stream/**", "zk2/h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend/*/@state/**", "zk2/h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend/*/@op/**", "zk2/h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend/@zk/**"] },
    // consume (h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend): §11.1 Consume: subscribe or GET on what the bindings name, one selector per bound provider (R1), R2's parameter bindings applied
    { id: "consume-in:h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend", permission: "allow", flows: ["ingress"],
      messages: ["declare_subscriber", "query"],
      key_exprs: ["zk2/*/tc/tc.netem.v1/events/**", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netem.v1/state/**", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netem.v1/stream/**", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netif.v1/state/**", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netif.v1/stream/**", "zk2/*/tc/tc.scenario.v1/state/**"] },
    // consume (h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend): §11.1 Consume, egress: the samples and replies those selectors receive
    { id: "consume-out:h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend", permission: "allow", flows: ["egress"],
      messages: ["put", "delete", "reply"],
      key_exprs: ["zk2/*/tc/tc.netem.v1/events/**", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netem.v1/state/**", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netem.v1/stream/**", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netif.v1/state/**", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netif.v1/stream/**", "zk2/*/tc/tc.scenario.v1/state/**"] },
    // presence (h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend): §11.1 Consume and Call (0.8), §8.1: liveliness reads on the `@zk` subtree of each service named. A refused read is answered complete and empty, so a reader the grants refuse would attribute silence to absence (§11.3)
    { id: "presence-in:h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend", permission: "allow", flows: ["ingress"],
      messages: ["declare_liveliness_subscriber", "liveliness_query"],
      key_exprs: ["zk2/*/tc/@zk/**"] },
    // presence (h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend): §11.1 (0.8), §8.1, egress: the tokens those reads receive
    { id: "presence-out:h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend", permission: "allow", flows: ["egress"],
      messages: ["liveliness_token"],
      key_exprs: ["zk2/*/tc/@zk/**"] },
    // call (h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend): §11.1 Call: query on the specific `…/@op/<op>` keys called
    { id: "call-in:h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend", permission: "allow", flows: ["ingress"],
      messages: ["query"],
      key_exprs: ["zk2/*/tc/tc.netif.v1/@op/diagnostics", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netif.v1/@op/interfaces/*/*/set", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netem.v1/@op/config/*/*/set", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netem.v1/@op/plug/*/*/set", "zk2/*/tc/tc.scenario.v1/@op/execution/*/*/control", "zk2/*/tc/tc.scenario.v1/@op/scenarios/put", "zk2/*/tc/tc.scenario.v1/@op/scenarios/*/remove"] },
    // call (h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend): §11.1 Call, egress: the replies, a server's refusal included (O2, O3)
    { id: "call-out:h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend", permission: "allow", flows: ["egress"],
      messages: ["reply"],
      key_exprs: ["zk2/*/tc/tc.netif.v1/@op/diagnostics", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netif.v1/@op/interfaces/*/*/set", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netem.v1/@op/config/*/*/set", "zk2/*/tc/tc.netem.v1/@op/plug/*/*/set", "zk2/*/tc/tc.scenario.v1/@op/execution/*/*/control", "zk2/*/tc/tc.scenario.v1/@op/scenarios/put", "zk2/*/tc/tc.scenario.v1/@op/scenarios/*/remove"] },
    // contracts: §11.1: contract bundles are open, any principal may hold or fetch `zk2/@zk/contract/**`, because the hash is the check (§8.4)
    { id: "contracts-in", permission: "allow", flows: ["ingress"],
      messages: ["declare_queryable", "reply", "query"],
      key_exprs: ["zk2/@zk/contract/**"] },
    // contracts: §11.1: contract bundles are open, any principal may hold or fetch `zk2/@zk/contract/**`, because the hash is the check (§8.4)
    { id: "contracts-out", permission: "allow", flows: ["egress"],
      messages: ["query", "reply"],
      key_exprs: ["zk2/@zk/contract/**"] },
  ],
  subjects: [
    { id: "tc-h-3fa9c2d41b7e", usernames: ["tc-h-3fa9c2d41b7e"] },  // runs h-3fa9c2d41b7e/tc
    { id: "tc-h-20609002f7b6", usernames: ["tc-h-20609002f7b6"] },  // runs h-20609002f7b6/tc
    { id: "tcgui-frontend", usernames: ["tcgui-frontend"] },  // runs h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend
  ],
  policies: [
    { id: "tc-h-3fa9c2d41b7e", rules: ["own-in:h-3fa9c2d41b7e/tc", "own-out:h-3fa9c2d41b7e/tc", "fan-in:h-3fa9c2d41b7e/tc", "fan-in-reply:h-3fa9c2d41b7e/tc", "contracts-in", "contracts-out"],
      subjects: ["tc-h-3fa9c2d41b7e"] },
    { id: "tc-h-20609002f7b6", rules: ["own-in:h-20609002f7b6/tc", "own-out:h-20609002f7b6/tc", "fan-in:h-20609002f7b6/tc", "fan-in-reply:h-20609002f7b6/tc", "contracts-in", "contracts-out"],
      subjects: ["tc-h-20609002f7b6"] },
    { id: "tcgui-frontend", rules: ["own-in:h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend", "own-out:h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend", "consume-in:h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend", "consume-out:h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend", "presence-in:h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend", "presence-out:h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend", "call-in:h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend", "call-out:h-0123456789ab/tcgui-frontend", "contracts-in", "contracts-out"],
      subjects: ["tcgui-frontend"] },
  ],
},

```

```console
$ zenctl acl gen --enrollment ../examples/zk2/acl/tcgui.enrollment.toml --contracts ../examples/zk2/.history --json5 --format json
? 2
error: the argument '--json5' cannot be used with '--format <FORMAT>'

--json5 emits a foreign document format — somebody else's schema — while --format chooses among zenctl's own three renderings of a report. Drop one.

Usage: zenctl <COMMAND>

For more information, try '--help'.

```

Under `--default-permission allow`, zenoh evaluates no allow rule, so each
grant compiles into denies of its complement (§11.2, D13): every other
service's writes, and every surface of theirs the principal's grants do not
name, enumerated from the contracts. The frontend is granted every surface
of both backends; only Own's complement is left to deny it. The admin
space is denied to every principal's queryables (#684). The posture's facts
are said, never assumed.

