A file that is not there is a question that could not be asked: exit 2,
never a 1 claiming the block differs.

```console
$ zenctl acl gen --enrollment ../examples/zk2/acl/tcgui.enrollment.toml --contracts ../examples/zk2/.history --check --against tests/cmd/fixtures/acl/no-such-router.json5
? 2
Error: tests/cmd/fixtures/acl/no-such-router.json5: zenoh refused the config: No such file or directory (os error 2)
acl gen --check: the question could not be asked — exit 2, the reserved non-verdict (1 here would claim a verdict this run never reached)

```

An enrollment that does not load is refused before anything is planned:
v1's roles and origins are not zk2's.

```console
$ zenctl acl gen --enrollment tests/cmd/fixtures/acl/enrollment-v1.toml --contracts ../examples/zk2/.history
? 2
Error: enrollment tests/cmd/fixtures/acl/enrollment-v1.toml: TOML parse error at line 6, column 1
  |
6 | origin = "h-3fa9c2d41b7e"
  | ^^^^^^
unknown field `origin`, expected one of `id`, `cn`, `user`, `zid`, `services`, `archives`, `tools`

```

A principal the plan cannot place is refused, never dropped: named with its
reason and the fact it rests on, left out of subjects and policies, and the
plan emitted around it. Exit 1: rows were refused.

```console
$ zenctl acl gen --enrollment tests/cmd/fixtures/acl/enrollment-refused.toml --contracts ../examples/zk2/.history --format ndjson
? 1
{"contracts":["tc.netif.v1@sha256:4f531ebec4c4eee015c18f11aefbce9138b413cfdca6bf6b777ea0eb6f43b4e0"],"default_permission":"deny","namespace":"","notes":[{"text":"REFUSED bench-rig: zid /"a1b2c3d4/": a zid is not backed by authentication, so it binds nothing; bind the principal by `user` or `cn` (§11.3: `zids` subjects are unauthenticated; principals are bound by certificate CN or username), left out of subjects and policies"},{"text":"REFUSED ghost: it runs service /"h9/tc/", which the enrollment does not declare (§11.1), left out of subjects and policies"}],"report":"acl-plan"}
{"cite":"§11.1 Own: the service puts, deletes, serves and declares tokens under its prefix, each verbatim subtree spelled out because `**` never crosses one (§1.3), its `@adv` subtrees where it uses advanced publication (§2.5); reply covers its answers to queries on its own keys","flows":["ingress"],"grant":"own","holder":"h1/tc","id":"own-in:h1/tc","key_exprs":["zk2/h1/tc/**","zk2/h1/tc/*/@stream/**","zk2/h1/tc/*/@state/**","zk2/h1/tc/*/@op/**","zk2/h1/tc/@zk/**"],"messages":["put","delete","declare_queryable","reply","liveliness_token"],"permission":"allow","row":"rule"}
{"cite":"§11.1 Own, egress: queries and subscriptions on its own keys reach it, so a queryable is asked and a publisher learns of interest (spike S14)","flows":["egress"],"grant":"own","holder":"h1/tc","id":"own-out:h1/tc","key_exprs":["zk2/h1/tc/**","zk2/h1/tc/*/@stream/**","zk2/h1/tc/*/@state/**","zk2/h1/tc/*/@op/**","zk2/h1/tc/@zk/**"],"messages":["query","declare_subscriber"],"permission":"allow","row":"rule"}
{"cite":"§11.1: contract bundles are open, any principal may hold or fetch `zk2/@zk/contract/**`, because the hash is the check (§8.4)","flows":["ingress"],"grant":"contracts","id":"contracts-in","key_exprs":["zk2/@zk/contract/**"],"messages":["declare_queryable","reply","query"],"permission":"allow","row":"rule"}
{"cite":"§11.1: contract bundles are open, any principal may hold or fetch `zk2/@zk/contract/**`, because the hash is the check (§8.4)","flows":["egress"],"grant":"contracts","id":"contracts-out","key_exprs":["zk2/@zk/contract/**"],"messages":["query","reply"],"permission":"allow","row":"rule"}
